WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Oil sands operations contribute significant carbon emissions in Canada. So the six largest companies have teamed up to make strides on the path to NetZero. Investing in technology and innovation. Already cut emissions in average 22% per barrel. Working with governments to create and protect jobs. Developing one of the world's largest carbon capture and storage facilities. Our NetZero plan is in motion and we're making progress on multiple pathways. See our plan in action at pathwaysalliance.ca
加拿大油砂开采贡献了大量的碳排放，因此六大公司携手合作，在迈向净零排放的道路上取得进展。他们投资于技术和创新，每桶原油的平均排放量已经减少了22%，并与政府合作创造和保护就业岗位，还开发了世界上最大的碳捕集与储存设施之一。我们的净零计划正在实施中，并且我们在多个途径上都取得了进展。请访问 pathwaysalliance.ca 亲眼见证我们的计划。

2
00:00:43.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. It was around dinner time on Friday, May 21, 2010, when Julie Kibuwishi received a text message. Can you come over tonight at midnight alone? Very upset. Need to talk. Julie typed a reply asking what was the matter. After making her promise that she wouldn't tell anyone, the sender explained that they were hurting due to some bad family crap.
我们的节目涉及严重且往往令人痛苦的事件。如果您在任何时候觉得需要支持，请联系您当地的危机中心。有关机密支持的建议电话号码，请查看您使用的应用上或我们网站上的本集节目说明。那是2010年5月21日星期五的晚餐时间左右，朱莉·基布伊什（Julie Kibuwishi）收到了一条短信：“今晚能一个人过来吗？我很心烦，需要聊聊。”朱莉打字回复询问出了什么事。在让她保证不告诉任何人后，发信人解释说他们因为一些糟糕的家庭破事而感到痛苦。

3
00:01:33.000 --> 00:02:27.000
A short while later, Julie's cell phone lit up again. Where are you? Can you come by? I don't want to be up late. It was approaching midnight when Julie pulled up to the Camden-Martinac apartments in the Californian city of Costa Mesa. The sprawling residential complex consisted of multiple low-rise buildings interspersed with winding walkways and palm trees. After parking her car, Julie headed towards one of the buildings while texting, Hey buddy, I am here. I am walking to your place. Then, as she reached the right floor, she messaged her brother, Taka, to let him know she'd arrived safely at her destination. As Julie typed, she heard a strange sound from the other side of an apartment door.
不久之后，朱莉的手机再次亮起：“你在哪？能过来吗？我不想熬夜。”接近午夜时分，朱莉将车停在了加利福尼亚州科斯塔梅萨市的卡姆登-马蒂纳克（Camden-Martinac）公寓楼外。这个错落有致的住宅区由多栋低层建筑组成，其间点缀着蜿蜒的小路和棕榈树。停好车后，朱莉一边发短信“嘿，老兄，我到了。我正朝你家走去”，一边走向其中一栋建筑。接着，当她到达正确的楼层时，她给哥哥塔卡（Taka）发了消息，告知他自己已经安全到达目的地。就在朱莉打字的时候，她听到公寓门的那头传来了奇怪的声音。

4
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:59.000
It sounded like a person sobbing. Signing off her message to Taka, Julie wrote, Sam is crying. It's not good. A few hours earlier, 23-year-old Julie Kibuwishi had been out of town. She said, I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
听起来像是一个人在抽泣。朱莉结束了给塔卡的留言，写道：“萨姆在哭，情况不太妙。”几小时前，23岁的朱莉·基布伊什还一直在外地。“我很抱歉。我很抱歉。我很抱歉。”

5
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:31.000
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. A few hours earlier, 23-year-old Julie Kibuwishi had been out with her brother Taka and his fiance in Long Beach, not far from where she lived in Irvine, Orange County. The trio were dining at a Thai restaurant near Taka's home. It was a special occasion. Taka and his fiance had a very important request to make of Julie.
“我很抱歉。我很抱歉。我很抱歉。”几小时前，23岁的朱莉·基布伊什还和她的哥哥塔卡以及他的未婚妻在长滩外出，离她居住的橙县尔湾不远。三人在塔卡家附近的一家泰国餐厅用餐。这是一个特殊的日子，塔卡和他的未婚妻对朱莉有一个非常重要的请求。

6
00:03:31.000 --> 00:04:09.000
Julie was born on Valentine's Day in 1987, and others jokingly said that this was the reason she was a hopeless romantic. So, when Julie was asked to be a bridesmaid at her brother's upcoming wedding, she was overcome with the joy. After she happily accepted the offer, Taka handed his sister a tiara. It was both a gift and the finishing touch for her bridesmaid outfit. Julie put it on at once. After dinner, the trio headed back to Taka's home to continue chatting.
朱莉于1987年的情人节出生，别人开玩笑说这就是她无可救药地充满浪漫主义情怀的原因。因此，当朱莉被邀请在她哥哥即将到来的婚礼上担任伴娘时，她欣喜若狂。在她愉快地接受了这个请求后，塔卡递给他的妹妹一顶头饰。这既是一份礼物，也是她伴娘装扮的点睛之笔。朱莉立刻戴上了它。晚餐后，三人回到塔卡的家继续聊天。

7
00:04:09.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Julie wasn't planning on staying long though. During dinner, her red Samsung cellphone had lit up with text messages from a close friend named Sam Hare. The two had met at Orange Coast Community College where they both took anthropology. Julie had tutored Sam in the subject, helping him achieve an A in that class. According to Sam's texts, he was having a rough night. After some back and forth, Julie told Sam she would leave her brother's house to visit him right away. She respected Sam's request to come alone, and after a short drive, Julie arrived at the Camden Martinique apartments in Costa Mesa where Sam lived.
不过，朱莉并没有打算待太久。晚饭期间，她的红色三星手机闪烁着来自一位名叫萨姆·黑尔（Sam Hare）的密友的短信。两人是在橙海岸社区学院认识的，当时他们都选修了人类学。朱莉曾在这门课上辅导过萨姆，帮他在那门课上取得了A的成绩。根据萨姆的短信，他度过了一个糟糕的夜晚。经过一番微信往返，朱莉告诉萨姆她会离开哥哥家立刻去探望他。她尊重萨姆独自前来的请求，经过短暂的车程，朱莉抵达了萨姆居住的位于科斯塔梅萨的卡姆登马提尼克公寓。

8
00:05:00.000 --> 00:06:00.000
The following morning, Junco Kibuishi stood at the door to her daughter Julie's bedroom. The bed inside had not been slept in, and there was no sign of Julie anywhere else in the house. It wasn't like Julie to disappear without telling her parents where she would be. Family had always been of the utmost importance to her. Born into a close-knit Japanese-American household, Julie was the third of four children and had two older brothers. When Julie's mother Junco was pregnant with her, she was told that her third child would be a boy as well. Julie was therefore an unexpected, though happy surprise to her parents. They named her Juri, but as their first daughter grew older, she was more commonly known to her friends by the Americanized version of her name, Julie.
第二天早上，纯子·基布伊什（Junco Kibuishi）站在女儿朱莉的卧室门口。里面的床没有被睡过，屋里其他地方也没有朱莉的踪影。朱莉向来不会在不告诉父母去哪里的情况下消失。家庭对她来说一直是最重要的。朱莉出生在一个关系紧密的日裔美国家庭，是四个孩子中的老三，有两个哥哥。当朱莉的母亲纯子怀着她时，有人告诉她第三个孩子也会是个男孩。因此，对父母来说，朱莉是一个意外却充满喜悦的惊喜。他们给她起名叫Juri，但随着大女儿的长大，朋友们更习惯用她名字的美国化称呼——朱莉。

9
00:06:00.000 --> 00:07:22.000
Now unable to find Julie anywhere, Junco followed up with her friends, but none could shed any light on where she might be. When texts and calls to Julie's cell phone continued to go unanswered, Junco was certain something was wrong and contacted the police. At the same time that Julie's family were worrying about her, a couple who lived in the Orange County neighborhood of Anaheim Hills were wondering where their son might be. Steve and Raquel Herr had been expecting a visit from their only child, Samuel, better known as Sam. He spent many weekends with his parents, who were only a 30-minute drive away from his Costa Mesa apartment. Raquel had spoken with Sam over the phone around lunchtime the previous day, and he hadn't given any indication that he intended to change his plans. The couple tried calling Sam periodically throughout the day, but his cell phone was switched off. This seemed odd. They had never known Sam to turn off his phone. By late evening, Steve Herr was standing at the front door to his son's apartment.
现在到处都找不到朱莉，纯子便联系了她的朋友们，但没有人能透露她可能在哪里。当打给朱莉手机的短信和电话依然无人接听时，纯子确信出事了，于是联系了警方。就在朱莉的家人为她担心的同时，一对住在橙县安纳海姆山社区的夫妇正在纳闷他们的儿子会在哪。史蒂夫·黑尔（Steve Herr）和拉奎尔·黑尔（Raquel Herr）一直期待着他们唯一的孩子塞缪尔（Samuel，人称萨姆）来拜访。他经常和父母度过周末，父母的家距离他在科斯塔梅萨的公寓只有30分钟的车程。前一天午餐时间左右，拉奎尔曾通过电话与萨姆交谈过，他当时没有表现出任何要改变计划的迹象。这对夫妇一整天都在断断续续地给萨姆打电话，但他的手机关机了。这显得很奇怪。他们从来没遇到过萨姆关机的情况。到了深夜，史蒂夫·黑尔站在了儿子公寓的前门外。

10
00:07:22.000 --> 00:08:24.000
Using a spare key Sam had given him, Steve let himself in to check that everything was alright. The lights were on, but all was quiet. Nothing looked out of place. Sam's apartment was a typical sparsely furnished bachelor pad. His acoustic guitar was perched in its stand in a lounge. Some blankets were folded up at the end of the sofa, and textbooks sat on a bookcase. Everything was neat and tidy. In the kitchen, some washed dishes had been left on a drying rack, and mail sat stacked on a countertop. Empty beer bottles were scattered by the barbecue out on the patio. Despite the seemingly normal scene in front of him, Steve felt strange, as though someone else were in the apartment with him. He called out his son's name, Sammy.
史蒂夫用萨姆给他的备用钥匙打开门，进去检查一切是否安好。灯亮着，但四周一片寂静。没有什么东西看起来不妥。萨姆的公寓是一个典型的陈设简陋的单身汉居所。他的原声吉他立在休息室的支架上，沙发头叠着几条毯子，书架上放着教科书。一切都整洁有序。在厨房里，一些洗好的盘子放在沥水架上，台面上堆着信件。露台的烧烤炉旁散落着空啤酒瓶。尽管眼前的场景看起来很正常，但史蒂夫觉得很奇怪，仿佛公寓里还有别的人。他大声喊着儿子的名字：“萨姆。”

11
00:08:24.000 --> 00:09:12.000
Then, as Steve looked into Sam's bedroom, he was met with a horrifying sight. Alongside Sam's messy and unmade bed was a young woman. She was kneeling, her torso sprawled over the mattress, and her lower legs resting on the floor. Her jeans had been cut at the waistband and down through the seat, before being ripped down around her knees. A message had been scribbled in black marker across the back of a grey top she was still wearing. It read, quote, All yours, fuck you. The back of her head was bloody, as were the sheets beneath her.
接着，当史蒂夫朝萨姆的卧室看去时，他看到了恐怖的一幕。在萨姆凌乱且未整理的床铺旁躺着一名年轻女子。她跪着，上半身趴在床垫上，小腿贴着地板。她的牛仔裤在腰带处被剪开，一直剪到臀部，然后被撕扯到膝盖周围。她身上穿的一件灰色上衣的背面用黑色马克笔潦草地写着一句话。上面写着，引述：“全归你了，操你妈。”她脑后满是鲜血，底下的床单也是如此。

12
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Steve saw what he recognized as a gunshot wound in her scalp. Sitting on top of her head in her long matted black hair was a tiara. Steve knew without a doubt that the woman was dead. Panicked, he pulled out his cell phone and dialed 911. When the operator answered, he cried out in a distraught voice. There's a body in my son's apartment. Steve recognized the deceased woman as his son's close friend and anthropology tutor, Julie Kibuishi. He had met Julie before and thought she was a lovely young woman.
史蒂夫看到他认出是头皮上的枪伤。她那长而打结的黑发顶部戴着一顶头饰。史蒂夫毫不怀疑这个女人已经死了。惊慌失措之下，他掏出手机拨打了911。接线员接听时，他痛苦地哭喊道：“我儿子的公寓里有一具尸体。”史蒂夫认出死者是他儿子的密友兼人类学导师朱莉·基布伊什。他以前见过朱莉，觉得她是个可爱的年轻女子。

13
00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:55.000
Noting how well she got on with Sam, Steve later asked his son if there was a romantic connection between them. Sam had dismissed the notion, telling his father that Julie was more like a sister to him. But it looked as though some sort of sexual activity had taken place in Sam's room. When police arrived on the scene, they made the same observation. The way Julie's body was posed and the aggressive removal of her pants indicated that she had been sexually assaulted, then brutally executed. An autopsy later revealed Julie had been shot twice in the head. The message that had been scrawled on her back, or yours, fuck you, seemed pointed, as though directed at a particular person. Investigators suspected a love triangle.
注意到她和萨姆相处得很好，史蒂夫后来问他的儿子他们之间是否有恋情。萨姆对此不以为然，告诉父亲朱莉对她来说更像是妹妹。但看起来萨姆的房间里似乎发生某种性行为。当警察到达现场时，他们也做出了同样的观察。朱莉尸体呈现的姿势以及裤子被粗暴脱下的方式表明她曾遭受性侵，随后被残忍处决。尸检后来显示朱莉头部中了两枪。写在她背上的那句话“全归你了，操你妈”似乎意有所指，仿佛是针对特定的人。调查人员怀疑这是一起三角恋。

14
00:10:55.000 --> 00:12:05.000
Most likely, Sam had been competing for Julie's affections with another individual. Upon searching Sam's room, they found what appeared to be a sex manual, as well as a soldier's handbook. The latter made sense. Prior to enrolling at college when he was 26 years old, Sam Hare had served in the United States Army's 173rd Airborne Brigade Combat Team. He had been sent to Afghanistan and spent much of his time there fighting on the border with Pakistan, in a particularly dangerous region that was constantly under fire. When he returned to the US, Sam exhibited symptoms of post-traumatic stress disorder, suffering from regular nightmares where he was trapped in a foxhole while insurgents bore down on him. Eager to move on with his life, he enrolled in college so he could obtain a degree. In addition to the books, investigators recovered a clean knife with a wide, partially serrated blade.
最有可能的是，萨姆一直在与另一个人争夺朱莉的爱慕。在搜查萨姆的房间时，他们发现了一本疑似性爱手册以及一本士兵手册。后者说得通。萨姆·黑尔在26岁入读大学之前，曾在美国陆军第173空降旅战斗队服役。他被派往阿富汗，大部分时间都在巴基斯坦边境作战，那是一个不断遭到炮火袭击的极其危险的地区。回到美国后，萨姆表现出创伤后应激障碍的症状，经常做噩梦，梦见自己被困在散兵坑里，而叛乱分子步步紧逼。急于继续生活，他考入大学以获取学位。除了书籍之外，调查人员还找到了一把干净的刀，刀刃很宽，带有部分锯齿。

15
00:12:05.000 --> 00:13:03.000
Julie's handbag was found in the kitchen with her driver's license and cell phone inside. An examination of Julie's phone revealed how Sam had repeatedly reached out to her the previous night. In a series of text messages, he'd begged her to come over to his place while also insisting that she come alone and tell no one. Investigators noted how Sam had reassured Julie that his desire to see her wasn't sexual, writing in one message, Please, no sex. Sam's cell phone, wallet and passport were nowhere to be found. His car, a white Pontiac, was also missing. Investigators ran a background check on Sam Hare to find out who exactly they were dealing with.
朱莉的手提包在厨房里被发现，里面有她的驾照和手机。对朱莉手机的检查显示前一晚萨姆是如何多次联系她的。在一系列短信中，他恳求她去他家，同时坚持要她一个人来，并且不要告诉任何人。调查人员注意到萨姆是如何向朱莉保证他想见她并非出于性欲，他在一条消息中写道：“求你了，不要发生性行为。”萨姆的手机、钱包和护照都不翼而飞。他的车，一辆白色的庞蒂亚克，也不见了。调查人员对萨姆·黑尔进行了背景调查，以弄清楚他们究竟在和谁打交道。

16
00:13:03.000 --> 00:14:04.000
As well as learning that Sam was an army veteran with extensive combat experience, they made another, more disturbing discovery. Eight years earlier in 2002, Sam Hare had been charged with murder. At the time, Sam was 18 years old. He had been friends with another young man named Byron Benito who had gang affiliations. Authorities said that after some gang members suspected Byron of shooting one of their friends, Sam Hare helped them by luring Byron to a secluded industrial estate. According to police, after Sam and Byron arrived there, a group of assailants attacked Byron, stabbing and beating him to death. For his role in the plot, Sam Hare was charged with murder and spent almost a year in custody before going to trial in 2004.
在得知萨姆是一名拥有丰富作战经验的退役军人之外，他们还有了另一个更令人不安的发现。八年前的2002年，萨姆·黑尔曾被指控谋杀。当时萨姆18岁。他曾与另一个有黑帮背景的年轻男子拜伦·贝尼托（Byron Benito）是朋友。当局表示，在一些黑帮成员怀疑拜伦枪杀了一名同伴后，萨姆·黑尔通过诱骗拜伦到一个偏僻的工业园区协助了他们。据警方称，萨姆和拜伦到达那里后，一群袭击者袭击了拜伦，将其刺死并殴打致死。因在阴谋中扮演的角色，萨姆·黑尔被控谋杀，在候审前被关押了近一年，直到2004年出庭受审。

17
00:14:04.000 --> 00:15:20.000
The prosecution argued that while Sam hadn't physically hurt Byron, he had taken him to the side of his death with full knowledge of what would unfold. Unconvinced that these actions proved Sam guilty of murder, a jury ultimately acquitted him. Relieved and determined to start a new life, Sam enlisted in the army and went on to become a decorated veteran. Despite his full exoneration, Sam's history was notable to the detectives investigating him for the murder of Julie Kibuwishi almost a decade later. Similarities between the two crimes were clear. Byron and Julie were close friends of Sam and both had met a violent end after Sam lured them to a predetermined destination. At this point, locating Sam became a matter of public safety. Physically fit and strongly built, Sam was more than capable of defending himself if necessary. Then there was his military combat experience as well as the likelihood that he was armed with a gun.
控方辩称，虽然萨姆没有对拜伦造成物理伤害，但他是在完全知晓会发生什么的情况下将拜伦带到了丧命之地。由于不确信这些行为证明萨姆犯有谋杀罪，陪审团最终宣告他无罪。如释重负并决心开始新生活的萨姆参军入伍，后来成为了一名荣立战功的退役军人。尽管已被完全开脱，但萨姆的过往对于近十年后调查朱莉·基布伊什谋杀案的侦探来说依然引人注目。两起罪行的相似之处显而易见。拜伦和朱莉都是萨姆的密友，在萨姆将他们诱骗至预定地点后，两人都迎来了暴力的结局。此时，找到萨姆成了一个公共安全问题。身体健硕、体格强壮的萨姆在必要时完全有能力保护自己。然后还有他的军事战斗经验，以及他很可能持有枪支的可能性。

18
00:15:20.000 --> 00:16:26.000
Investigators had to move quickly. They interviewed everyone who knew Sam, including a number of neighbors who lived in the Camden-Martinac apartments. Due to most of the residents being college students around the same age, the apartments had a thriving social scene and many of the people who lived there were friendly with one another. One man who lived a couple of floors below Sam said he'd seen him the afternoon before Julie was murdered. Sam had helped him move some heavy items, then he'd left Camden-Martinac with a man Sam's neighbor had never seen before. The man was white and wore a black baseball cap. The neighbor's fiance confirmed this sighting, adding that the man didn't live at the apartments and she had never seen him before. Meanwhile, Sam's father, Steve, was struggling with the sudden disappearance of his son.
调查人员必须迅速行动。他们采访了所有认识萨姆的人，包括住在卡姆登-马蒂纳克公寓的一群邻居。由于大多数居民都是年纪相仿的大学生，公寓有着繁荣的社交圈，许多住在那里的人彼此都很友好。一个住在萨姆楼下几层的男子说，他在朱莉被谋杀的前一天下午见过他。萨姆曾帮他搬了一些重物，然后和另一个萨姆的邻居从未见过的人离开了卡姆登-马蒂纳克。那名男子是个白人，戴着黑色棒球帽。邻居的未婚妻证实了这次目击，并补充说该男子不住在公寓里，她以前从未见过他。与此同时，萨姆的父亲史蒂夫正艰难面对儿子突如其来的失踪。

19
00:16:26.000 --> 00:17:26.000
Determined to track him down, he began carrying out his own private investigation. Sam had previously provided his father with all of his online banking details and passwords in case of an emergency. On Monday, May 24, when Sam had been missing for two days, Steve logged into his son's bank account. Almost right away, Steve noticed that there had been lots of activity. Over the past few days, Sam had repeatedly withdrawn funds from an ATM in Long Beach. Each time, he opted to take out $400, the maximum amount his bank permitted him to withdraw in a day. Overall, these increments had added up to almost $2,000. Steve then drove to Long Beach in the hopes of catching Sam in the act.
为了找到他，他开始进行自己的私下调查。萨姆此前曾将自己所有的网上银行详细信息和密码提供给父亲，以防万一。5月24日星期一，当萨姆失踪已经两天时，史蒂夫登录了儿子的银行账户。几乎立刻，史蒂夫注意到有大量的活动。在过去的几天里，萨姆多次从长滩的一台自动取款机提取资金。每次，他都选择取出400美元，这是他的银行允许一天内取款的最大额度。总体而言，这些零星的金额加起来近2000美元。史蒂夫随后开车前往长滩，希望能抓萨姆一个现行。

20
00:17:26.000 --> 00:18:17.000
He staked out the city's ATMs but didn't see his son. Then he drove around the area's streets and roads, keeping a lookout for Sam's white Pontiac. There was no sign of it. Suddenly, a notification came through on Steve's phone from Sam's bank. Sam's bank card had just been used to order some pizzas from a Long Beach pizza parlor named Echoes. Steve rushed to the restaurant. It sat along a busy six-lane thoroughfare with tables and umbrellas set out along the pavement for outdoor dining. Steve parked in front of Echoes and alternated between watching its glass door entrance and keeping an eye out for Sam's car.
他在该市的自动取款机旁蹲守，但没有看到儿子。然后他在该地区的街道和小路上开车巡视，寻找萨姆白色的庞蒂亚克。毫无踪影。突然，史蒂夫的手机上收到了来自萨姆银行的通知。萨姆的银行卡刚刚被用来从长滩一家名为“回声”（Echoes）的比萨店订购了一些比萨。史蒂夫冲向餐馆。它位于一条繁忙的六车道大道旁，人行道上摆着桌子和遮阳伞供户外用餐。史蒂夫把车停在“回声”门前，在监视其玻璃门入口和留意萨姆的车之间来回切换。

21
00:18:17.000 --> 00:19:19.000
He waited for an hour. Although other patrons came and went, his son never appeared. The case detectives had also gained access to Sam's banking records and were also keeping a watch on account activity. Like Steve, they had noted the repeated withdrawals being made from Long Beach. There had been four separate withdrawals from two different Chase Bank ATMs. The machines had cameras fitted inside and investigators were able to obtain the surveillance footage from both. Upon examining the footage recorded at the exact times Sam's card had been used, detectives were perplexed. Standing before the machine was a teenage boy. He was white and looked very young, dressed in a hoodie and a black baseball cap.
他等了一个小时。尽管其他顾客来来往往，但他的儿子始终没有出现。案件侦探也获取了萨姆的银行记录，并在监视账户活动。和史蒂夫一样，他们注意到了从长滩进行的反复提款。从两家不同的大通银行自动取款机进行了四次独立的提款。这些机器内部装有摄像头，调查人员能够从两处获取监控录像。在检查萨姆的卡被使用的准确时间录制的录像时，侦探们感到困惑。站在机器前的是一个十几岁的男孩。他是个白人，看起来非常年轻，穿着连帽衫和黑色棒球帽。

22
00:19:19.000 --> 00:20:25.000
Was this the individual in the black hat that Sam's neighbours had seen him with on the day of Julie's murder? The detectives didn't recognise him and nor did Sam's parents when they were shown a photo. Investigators contacted Echo's pizza parlor where Sam's card had been used to make a purchase and asked for the delivery address provided for that particular order. Once they had it, a full SWAT team descended on the property and a helicopter was dispatched for an aerial view. If Sam Hare was hiding inside, the investigators didn't want to take any chances. The last thing they needed was a hostage situation on their hands. Judging from the noises emanating from the house, a party was in full swing. When the occupants were ordered to open up, the teenage boy who had been caught on the ATMs camera opened the front door.
这就是朱莉被谋杀那天萨姆的邻居们看到的那个戴黑帽子的男子吗？侦探们不认识他，萨姆的父母在看到照片时也不认识。调查人员联系了使用萨姆的卡进行购买的“回声”比萨店，并索取了该特定订单提供的送货地址。一旦拿到地址，整支特警队便突袭了该物业，并派出一架直升机进行空中观察。如果萨姆·黑尔藏在里面，调查人员绝不愿冒险。他们最不需要的就是发生人质事件。从屋里传出的噪音判断，一场派对正在热烈进行。当勒令屋内的人开门时，那个被自动取款机摄像头拍到的十几岁男孩打开了前门。

23
00:20:25.000 --> 00:21:39.000
His name was Wesley and he was 17 years old. He lived there with his mother who was a drama teacher. Wesley was ordered out of the house along with his friends whom he'd invited over to play video games and instructed to get down on the ground. As he lay on the front lawn, officers filed inside to conduct a thorough search, determined that they would flush out Sam Hare from wherever he was hiding. After examining each room, it was clear Sam Hare wasn't in the house, but his debit card was. When confronted with Sam's debit card, Wesley denied having used it or even knowing anything about it. Are you sure about that, one of the officers asked? This card's tied to a homicide. Wesley's demeanor immediately changed. He looked visibly scared as he repeated the words, a homicide. It didn't take long for him to spill what he knew.
他的名字叫韦斯利（Wesley），今年17岁。他和当戏剧老师的母亲住在这里。韦斯利和被他请来玩电子游戏的朋一起被命令走出屋子，并被指示趴在地上。当他躺在前草坪上时，警官们排队进入屋内进行彻底搜查，决心无论萨姆·黑尔藏在哪里都要把他逼出来。在检查了每个房间后，很明显萨姆·黑尔不在屋里，但他的借记卡在。当面对萨姆的借记卡时，韦斯利否认自己使用过它，甚至否认对此事知情。“你确定吗？”其中一名警官问。“这张卡跟一桩凶杀案有关。”韦斯利的神态立刻变了。他看起来明显很害怕，重复着“凶杀案”这个词。没花多久他就吐露了他所知道的一切。

24
00:21:39.000 --> 00:22:51.000
Wesley didn't know Sam Hare. He had been withdrawing the money on behalf of someone else. 26-year-old Daniel Wozniak lived at the Camden-Martineke apartments, a couple of floors below Sam Hare's residence. He had held a few different jobs here and there, but his true passion was acting. Daniel's performances in community theatre productions had been positively received, and he was currently starring in the lead role in a several-month-long run of the musical Nine at an alternative theatre company in Orange County. He and Sam Hare became friendly after Daniel and his fiance, Rachel Buffett, a fellow aspiring actor, had moved into the complex several months earlier in February. They shared a circle of friends at Camden-Martineke and socialized regularly. Daniel was the downstairs neighbour who had mentioned seeing Sam leave with a man in a black baseball cap on the day of Julie Kibawishi's murder.
韦斯利不认识萨姆·黑尔。他是替别人取钱的。26岁的丹尼尔·沃兹尼亚克（Daniel Wozniak）住在卡姆登-马蒂尼克公寓，在萨姆·黑尔住所楼下几层。他在这里那里做过几份不同的工作，但他真正的热情是表演。丹尼尔在社区剧院制作中的表演受到了好评，目前他正在橙县的一家另类剧院公司长达数月的音乐剧《九》（Nine）中担任主角。他和萨姆·黑尔在丹尼尔和他的未婚妻蕾切尔·布菲（Rachel Buffett，同为有抱负的演员）几个月前的2月搬进该综合大楼后成为了朋友。他们在卡姆登-马蒂尼克分享了一个朋友圈并经常社交。丹尼尔就是那个提到在朱莉·基博伊什被谋杀当天看到萨姆和一个戴黑色棒球帽的男子离开的楼下邻居。

25
00:22:51.000 --> 00:23:59.000
Initially, this had appeared to be a helpful clue in the search for Sam. Now, investigators viewed Daniel's story far more critically. 17-year-old Wesley had since accused Daniel of supplying him with Sam's bank card under the order to drain the account. Was Daniel helping Sam evade authorities? If so, was he aware of what exactly his friend was running from? Detectives called Daniel Wozniak's cell phone seeking an explanation. He answered, but said that he couldn't speak with them that night because he was at his bachelor party. In two days' time, on Friday, May 28, Daniel was getting married, and he had gone out to a Japanese restaurant with a few friends to celebrate. Investigators didn't care. With Sam Hare still a threat to the public, they needed to speak with Daniel right away.
最初，这似乎是搜寻萨姆的一个有用线索。现在，调查人员对丹尼尔的故事持更批判的眼光。17岁的韦斯利此后指控丹尼尔给他提供了萨姆的银行卡，命令他掏空该账户。丹尼尔是在帮萨姆逃避当局吗？如果是这样，他是否知道他的朋友究竟在逃避什么？侦探们给丹尼尔·沃兹尼亚克的手机打去电话寻求解释。他接了电话，但说他今晚不能跟他们谈，因为他在参加单身汉派对。两天后的5月28日星期五，丹尼尔就要结婚了，他和小伙伴们出去到一家日本餐厅庆祝。侦探们可不管这些。由于萨姆·黑尔对公众仍然是个威胁，他们需要立刻与丹尼尔谈谈。

26
00:23:59.000 --> 00:25:11.000
Detective Jose Morales approached the beige single-story building that housed Sonami Sushi. Located on the Pacific Coast Highway in Huntington Beach, the restaurant often hosted parties, with its teppanyaki grill a popular attraction. Detective Morales entered the establishment alone. In his plain clothes, he wouldn't attract much attention. The detective walked through the front door and strolled around the bar area, scanning the room that Daniel Wozniak. He couldn't see him. Then, towards the back of the restaurant in a private banquet room, he spotted him. Daniel was dressed in khaki pants and a Hawaiian shirt, laughing as he drank sake with his friends. Detective Morales radioed for backup, and more officers soon arrived at the scene. They waited until Daniel had paid for the meal, then entered through the restaurant's rear door and filed into the banquet room.
何塞·莫拉莱斯侦探（Detective Jose Morales）走近了容纳“园美寿司”（Sonami Sushi）的米色单层建筑。该餐厅位于亨廷顿海滩的太平洋海岸公路旁，经常举办派对，其铁板烧烤架是一个受欢迎的吸引点。莫拉莱斯侦探独自进入了这家店。穿着便服的他不会引起太多注意。侦探走过前门，在酒吧区闲逛，扫视着丹尼尔·沃兹尼亚克。他看不到他。然后，在餐厅后面的一个私人宴会厅里，他发现了目标。丹尼尔穿着卡其裤和夏威夷衫，一边和朋友们喝清酒一边大笑。莫拉莱斯侦探用无线电呼叫增援，更多警察很快赶到了现场。他们等到丹尼尔付了餐费，然后从餐厅后门进入并排队走进了宴会厅。

27
00:25:11.000 --> 00:26:16.000
When Daniel looked up and saw them, all of the blood drained from his face. The detectives flashed their badges and patted Daniel down, before snapping a pair of handcuffs around his wrists. Then, he was escorted out of his own bachelor party and into a waiting police car. Once Daniel was seated in an interrogation room at Costa Mesa police station, he seemed more relaxed than he'd looked at the restaurant. Before questioning began, Daniel assured the interviewing detectives, I'm going to tell you everything, I'm sick of covering for Sam. He said he knew nothing about Julie Kibouishi's murder, but had been duped into helping supply funds for Sam Hare's escape. He also admitted that the man in the black baseball cap had never existed. He had invented him to cover up for himself.
当丹尼尔抬头看到他们时，他脸上的血色瞬间褪尽。侦探们亮出徽章，对丹尼尔进行搜身，然后把一副手铐“咔哒”一声铐在他的手腕上。随后，他被护送出自己的单身汉派对，带进了一辆等候的警车。一旦丹尼尔坐在科斯塔梅萨警察局的审讯室内，他似乎比在餐厅里时显得更加放松。在审问开始之前，丹尼尔向审讯侦探保证：“我会把一切都告诉你们，我厌倦了替萨姆打掩护。”他说他对朱莉·基博伊什的谋杀一无所知，但被愚弄去帮助为萨姆·黑尔的逃跑提供资金。他还承认那个戴黑色棒球帽的男子根本不存在。那是他编造出来为自己掩盖的。

28
00:26:16.000 --> 00:27:17.000
Daniel explained that Sam had called him the previous Friday morning, hours before he later attacked and killed Julie Kibouishi. Sam had offered to pay Daniel if he helped him out with the scheme. He was planning to drain his own bank account using a third party, and then intended to file a claim that his debit card had been stolen. His bank would have to refund what had been taken, and he'd get double the payout. The author was tempting. Daniel and his fiancee Rachel had little money. The community theatre shows they loved performing paid nothing, and they both worked odd jobs to get by. Somehow, they'd wound up severely in debt and months behind on their rent. What Sam was suggesting was illegal, but Daniel desperately wanted some cash.
丹尼尔解释说，萨姆在前一天周五早上，也就是他袭击并杀死朱莉·基博伊什几小时前给他打过电话。萨姆提出如果丹尼尔帮他搞定这个计划就付钱给他。他正计划通过第三方掏空自己的银行账户，然后打算提出借记卡被盗的索赔。他的银行必须退还被拿走的钱，他就能得到双倍的赔付。这个提议很诱人。丹尼尔和他的未婚妻蕾切尔没什么钱。他们热爱的社区剧院演出没有薪水，两人都靠打零工维生。不知何故，他们最终负债累累，房租拖欠了好几个月。萨姆建议的事情是非法的，但丹尼尔迫切想要一些现金。

29
00:27:17.000 --> 00:28:31.000
He agreed to participate, and Sam said he would stay clear of the ATMs being used to make withdrawals. That way, no one could say they had seen him there, and his face wouldn't be captured by the machine's cameras. Daniel asked his teenage friend Wesley, whom he'd met through their shared interest in theatre, to make the withdrawals. Daniel told Wesley he was working for a bail bonds agent, and that the card belonged to one of the agent's clients who had gone on the run after posting bail. He wanted Wesley's help to drain the client's account and had shown the teenager how to use the card and withdraw funds in $400 increments. He'd said it was vital that Wesley always wear a hat and sunglasses when he was at the ATM. Because Wesley was underage, Daniel believed he was less likely to get in trouble if he was caught. Daniel insisted that he had no idea where Sam Hare was now.
他同意参与，萨姆说他会避开用于提款的自动取款机。这样，没人会说在那里见过他，他的脸也不会被机器的摄像头捕捉到。丹尼尔请了他的少年朋友韦斯利（他通过对戏剧的共同兴趣认识了韦斯利）来取款。丹尼尔告诉韦斯利他在为保释金担保人工作，这张卡属于担保人的一个客户，该客户在交纳保释金后潜逃了。他想让韦斯利帮忙掏空客户的账户，并向这名少年展示了如何使用该卡并以400美元为增量提取资金。他说韦斯利在自动取款机前务必戴帽子和太阳镜，这一点至关重要。因为韦斯利未成年，丹尼尔相信如果被抓，他惹上麻烦的可能性较小。丹尼尔坚称他现在完全不知道萨姆·黑尔在哪里。

30
00:28:31.000 --> 00:29:29.000
Setting the credit fraud story aside, the interrogators changed the subject back to Julie Kibuishi. Did Daniel know anything about her murder? After initially saying he didn't, Daniel admitted that he did. Sam had told him all about it. On the evening of Friday, May 21, Daniel and his fiancee Rachel had performed on stage in the community theatre musical they were both in, before returning home for a quiet night watching TV on the couch. The next morning, Daniel was woken by a steady knocking at his front door. He opened it and saw Sam Hare standing outside, looking nervous. When Daniel asked if everything was alright, Sam replied, Not good, we're in trouble.
抛开信用卡诈骗的故事不谈，审讯人员将话题转回了朱莉·基布伊什。丹尼尔知道关于她谋杀的任何事情吗？在最初表示不知道之后，丹尼尔承认他确实知道。萨姆把一切都告诉了他。在5月21日星期五的晚上，丹尼尔和他的未婚妻蕾切尔在他们俩都参加的社区剧院音乐剧中进行了舞台表演，然后回家在沙发上安静地看电视度过了一晚。第二天早上，丹尼尔被一阵急促的敲门声吵醒。他打开门，看到萨姆·黑尔站在外面，神情紧张。当丹尼尔问一切是否安好时，萨姆回答：“不太好，我们有麻烦了。”

31
00:29:29.000 --> 00:30:26.000
Sam begged Daniel to get him out of Costa Mesa and handed over his laptop for safekeeping. Daniel told detectives where they could find the device in his apartment. The two got into Sam's white pondiac with Daniel behind the wheel. As they headed southbound down the Interstate 405 freeway, Sam suddenly made an admission. There's a body in my apartment. I shot somebody. I was not happy about it. It was a fit of rage and honestly, she had it coming. She, Daniel asked. Sam told him the victim was his good friend Julie Kibuishi. He had gotten drunk and high on ecstasy the night before and started scrolling through photos of Julie on social media.
萨姆恳求丹尼尔把他弄出科斯塔梅萨，并交出了他的笔记本电脑以妥善保管。丹尼尔告诉侦探他们可以在他公寓里的哪里找到这个设备。两人上了萨姆白色的庞蒂亚克，由丹尼尔开车。当他们向南开上405号州际高速公路时，萨姆突然坦白了。“我的公寓里有一具尸体。我枪杀了几个人。我对此并不高兴。这是一时冲动，老实说，她是咎由自取。”“她？”丹尼尔问。萨姆告诉他受害者是他的好朋友朱莉·基布伊什。他前一晚喝醉了并嗑了摇头丸，开始在社交媒体上浏览朱莉的照片。

32
00:30:26.000 --> 00:31:31.000
Becoming upset as he looked at the images, he started texting Julie, asking her to come over. When she arrived at his apartment, he propositioned her and she refused, so he shot and killed her. Daniel was shocked. He knew Julie from their social circle at Camden Martinique. She often joined the gatherings there as a friend of Sam's and now Sam had made him a partial accessory to her murder by asking for his help. Daniel pulled off the highway and began to shout, What the fuck? What have you got me into? What are you doing? Sam ordered Daniel not to tell anyone and threatened. I know where you live. You wrap me out. I'm going to fucking kill you. And better yet, I'm going to start with your wife. The two struck a deal.
看着这些图像时他感到心烦意乱，于是开始给朱莉发短信，要求她过来。当她到达他的公寓时，他向她求欢而她拒绝了，于是他开枪杀死了她。丹尼尔大为震惊。他从卡姆登-马蒂尼克社交圈里认识朱莉。她经常作为萨姆的朋友加入那里的聚会，现在萨姆通过寻求他的帮助，让他成了她谋杀案的部分同谋。丹尼尔将车驶离高速公路并开始大喊：“他妈的这是怎么回事？你把我卷入了什么？你在干什么？”萨姆命令丹尼尔不准告诉任何人并威胁道：“我知道你住哪。你要是把我供出来，我他妈的就杀了你。更糟的是，我要从你老婆开始下手。”两人达成了一笔交易。

33
00:31:31.000 --> 00:32:59.000
